## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical on-device CV with privacy constraints, latency pressure, and data privacy.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight models, ROI extraction, temporal reasoning
- Quantization, pruning, on-device inference
- Federated learning, differential privacy, privacy budgets
- Evaluation: latency, memory, F1/precision-recall under occlusion

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: frame window prep for on-device gesture model
function prepareWindow(frames) {
  const ROI = detectHandROI(frames[0]);
  const window = frames.slice(-16).map(f => crop(f, ROI));
  return stack(window);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure and mitigate drift when lighting changes across devices?
- How would you handle new gestures without retraining all devices?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates a practical monocular solution for tool manipulation that must handle new categories, operate under strict latency constraints, and support few-shot on-device adaptation in cluttered workshop environments.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 6-DoF pose estimation from 2D-3D correspondences
- Few-shot on-device adaptation using adapter modules
- Synthetic and real data strategy with domain randomization
- Real-time performance requirements and edge GPU optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
// PnP pose estimation sketch
function estimatePose2D3D(keypoints2D, model3D, camera) {
  // use perspective-n-point algorithm
  return cv.solvePnP(model3D, keypoints2D, camera.matrix, camera.distortion);
}
```
